.TH "cli-game-launcher" "1"
.SH NAME
.PP
cli-game-launcher - A minimal game launcher for your terminal

.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]cli-game-launcher\f[R] [COMMAND] [OPTIONS]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
cli-game-launcher is a command-line program that runs your game executables and saves the time spent playing. Tailored for people that just need a centralized way to launch both native games and games that run with Wine (via shell scripts).

.SH COMMANDS
.SS add
.TP
Add a new game.

.SS remove
.TP
Remove a game.

.SS run
.TP
Run a game.

.SS list
.TP
Print list of known games.

.SS hide
.TP
Toggle the visibility of a game.

.SS playtime
.TP
Show total playtime for each game.

.SS last-played
.TP
Show last played date for each game.

.SS last-two-weeks
.TP
Show total playtime in the last two weeks for each game.

.SS help
.TP
Print help information and exit.

.SH OPTIONS
.SS General Options:
.TP
-h, -help, --help
Print help text and exit.

.SS Game List Options:
.TP
-show-hidden=\f[I]BOOLEAN\f[R], --show-hidden=\f[I]BOOLEAN\f[R]
Show hidden games in the output. Either \fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse (default)\fR.
.TP
-only-hidden=\f[I]BOOLEAN\f[R], --only-hidden=\f[I]BOOLEAN\f[R]
Only show hidden games in the output. Either \fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse (default)\fR.

.SS Run Game Options:
.TP
-show-hidden=\f[I]BOOLEAN\f[R], --show-hidden=\f[I]BOOLEAN\f[R]
Show hidden games in the output. Either \fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse (default)\fR.

.SH FILES
\f[B]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cli-game-launcher/data.db\f[R] (Linux)
.PP
\f[B]/Users/user/Library/Application Support/cli-game-launcher/data.db\f[R] (macOS)
.PP
\f[B]%AppData%/cli-game-launcher/data.db\f[R] (Windows)
